    {
      "id": "eswrftf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SSC / SSC Important Exam Notes"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Article 32 is the very soul of the Constitution and the very heart of it.",
      "id": "q5eb4ek"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 1 defines India, that is Bharat, as a Union of States rather than a Federation of States.",
        "Part III (Articles 12-35) deals with Fundamental Rights, which are legally enforceable by courts.",
        "Article 32 grants the Right to Constitutional Remedies, allowing individuals to move the Supreme Court for enforcement of rights.",
        "Article 51A specifies Fundamental Duties, incorporated via the 42nd Amendment Act in 1976.",
        "Article 110 contains the definition of Money Bills, which can only be introduced in the Lok Sabha.",
        "Article 368 empowers Parliament to amend the Constitution and prescribes the procedure for doing so."
      ],
      "id": "u5n8d92"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ok1hroj",
      "content": "• Article 32 is called the 'Heart and Soul of the Constitution'."
    },
